        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L42"
      },
      "rationale": "Records its lookup in a nested block; with an established claimant it replays to the caller only the rows of the leaf's own document and the rows that are not a plain byte identity, so a sibling document that was read and ruled out is no input of the caller's result. When the leaf has no claimant it replays every row it opened — each sibling read in full and the exact direct JSON listing — so a performed negative lookup keeps depending on those files; the terminal task-root resolution is one of the admitted unrecorded B5 selectors and records no row; when the lookup raises it replays every row.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    }
  ],
